        rules: {
          objective: 'The first team to reach a cumulative score of 45 points wins.',
          gameplay: "1. Each hand consists of 5 tricks.\n2. Leading: The player to the dealer's left leads first.\n3. Following Suit: If a trump is led, you MUST follow suit if possible. If a non-trump is led, you may follow suit OR trump.",
          keyRules: [
            "The Five Fingers: The 5 of trumps can 'renege'â€”it don't have to be played even if a lower trump is led, unless a higher trump is played.",
            "Spoiling: If no team or player wins at least 3 tricks, the game is 'spoiled' and the pot/score carries over.",
            'Winning condition: The first team to reach a cumulative score of 45 points wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Protect your high trumps. Since the 5 and Jack are so powerful, don't waste them on a trick you can win with a lower card. Use them to 'pull' trumps from your opponents.",
          intermediate: "The Ace of Hearts is your wildcard. Never forget that it is a trump. It can be a devastating surprise if your opponent leads a suit they think you are void in, only for you to 'Ace' them.",
          advanced: 'Black Suit Logic: Remember that in black suits (Spades/Clubs), the 2 is higher than the 10. This frequently trips up beginners. Use your low-number black cards to win non-trump tricks.',
          tips: [
            'Rob the trump whenever possible. Getting that extra high card is often the difference between winning 2 tricks and winning 3.',
            "In partnerships, if your partner wins the first two tricks, 'throw' your best cards to help them secure the third trick and the round.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
